<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ fringe benefit tax prescribed rate reduced.</title>
<headline>NZ fringe benefit tax prescribed rate reduced.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The rate of interest used to calculate the fringe benefit value of low-interest employment-related loans has been reduced to 10.0 percent from 11.1 percent for the quarter commencing January 1, Finance and Revenue Minister Bill Birch said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Birch said the new rate was a reflection of the recent fall in market rates.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
</text>
